, by definition, unknown). So every live prediction from this model is out-of-distribution relative to its own training. The measured t0-window numbers above already reflect that (they are not a surprise), but this is 'best available', not 'production-ready' -- represent it that way. The operating_point (floor=0.0, mult=0.9) is the VAL-selected connected-causal decode point; it did NOT clear the 0.50 precision floor during selection (feasible=False, val P=0.270/R=0.259) -- it's the best-F1 fallback point, not a precision-guaranteed one.","issued_at_utc":"2026-08-08 14:26:22.865147+00:00","valid_from_utc":"2026-08-08 00:00:00","valid_to_utc":"2026-08-09 00:00:00","wfigs_date_current_utc":"2026-08-08 14:05:09+00:00","pixel_size_m":30,"veg_source":"refreshed_d4","physics_source":"eikonal_fbfm40","history_n_dates":21,"degraded_history":false,"containment_pct":1,"acres_wfigs":97538.21069475975}},{"type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"MultiPolygon","coordinates":[[[[-120.84519,47.98482],[-120.846,47.98482],[-120.846,47.98509],[-120.84519,47.98509],[-120.84519,47.98482]]],[[[-120.84479,47.98509],[-120.84519,47.98509],[-120.84519,47.98536],[-120.84479,47.98536],[-120.84479,47.98509]]],[[[-120.846,47.98509],[-120.8464,47.98509],[-120.8464,47.98536],[-120.846,47.98536],[-120.846,47.98509]]],[[[-120.8464,47.98644],[-120.8464,47.98536],[-120.8468,47.98536],[-120.8468,47.9859],[-120.8472,47.9859],[-120.8472,47.98617],[-120.84841,47.98617],[-120.84841,47.98644],[-120.8464,47.98644]]],[[[-120.84841,47.98644],[-120.84922,47.98644],[-120.84922,47.98671],[-120.84841,47.98671],[-120.84841,47.98644]]],[[[-120.85043,47.98724],[-120.84922,47.98724],[-120.84922,47.98671],[-120.84962,47.98671],[-120.84962,47.98697],[-120.85043,47.98697],[-120.85043,47.98724]]],[[[-120.85083,47.98724],[-120.85083,47.98697],[-120.85123,47.98697],[-120.85123,47.98724],[-120.85083,47.98724]]],[[[-120.85163,47.98778],[-120.85204,47.98778],[-120.85204,47.98805],[-120.85123,47.98805],[-120.85123,47.98724],[-120.85